# CUTAS web front end - build settings
# Copy to `.env.local` (development) or `.env.production` (build) only if you need to change a value.
# NEVER put secrets here: every VITE_* value is compiled into the public JavaScript bundle.
# Database passwords, JWT keys and SMTP credentials belong in the backend's .env only.

# Where the browser reaches the API.
# Leave unset (default "/api/v1") when the API is served on the same domain under /api, which is the
# case with the bundled nginx image, docker-compose, and the `npm run dev` proxy. Same-origin is the
# recommended set-up: the session cookie stays first-party and no CORS is needed.
# Set an absolute URL only when the API lives on a different domain, for example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.cutas.cut.ac.za/api/v1
# (then also add this site's origin to CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS in the backend .env)

# Development only: where `npm run dev` forwards /api requests (your local Django server).
# DEV_API_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8000
